I. ''trans.'' '''1.''' To bear witness to; certify; affirm to be true or genuine; declare the truth of in words or writing; especially, affirm in an official capacity: as, to ''attest'' the truth of a writing; to ''attest'' a copy of a document.
{{smaller block|The most monstrous fables . . . ''attested'' with the utmost solemnity. {{right|''Goldsmith'', Citizen of the World, xvi.}}}}
{{smaller block|This sale of a tract, twelve miles square, was formally ''attested'' at Manhattan. {{right|''Bancroft'', Hist. U. S., II. 44.}}}}
'''2.''' To make evident; vouch for; give proof or evidence of; manifest.
{{smaller block|<poem>The birds their notes renew, and bleating herds
''Attest'' their joy, that hill and valley rings.</poem>
{{right|''Milton'', P. L., ii. 495.}}}}
{{smaller block|The rancor of the disease ''attests'' the strength of the constitution. {{right|''Emerson'', Conduct of Life.}}}}
'''3.''' To call to witness; invoke as knowing or conscious. [Obsolete or archaic.]
{{smaller block|<poem>The sacred streams which heaven’s imperial state
''Attests'' in oaths, and fears to violate.</poem>
{{right|''Dryden.''}}}}
'''4.''' To put upon oath; swear in.
{{smaller block|If a proposed recruit, when taken before a justice of the peace, . . . should change his mind, he is dismissed upon paying a fine of twenty shillings, popularly called smart money; but if he does not, he is ''attested'', and after that, should he abscond, he is considered and punished as a deserter. {{right|''A. Fonblanque, Jr.''}}}}
{{smaller|'''Attesting witness''', a person who signs his name to an instrument to prove it, and for the purpose of identifying the maker or makers.}] ='''Syn. 1.''' To confirm, corroborate, support, authenticate, prove.}}
'''II.''' ''intrans.'' To bear witness; make an attestation: with ''to'': as, to ''attest to'' a statement or a document.

'''attest''' (a-test′), ''n.'' [< ''attest'', ''v.''] Witness; testimony; attestation. {{smaller|[Now chiefly used at the end of a document, as introductory to the name of one au-}}

